⚠ Why You Still See a Peer Warning
@apollo/server-plugin-landing-page-graphql-playground
✕ unmet peer @apollo/server@^4.0.0: found 5.4.0


This happens because:

The old GraphQL Playground plugin was built for Apollo v4

You are using Apollo v5

NestJS still includes that plugin as optional compatibility

But it does NOT break anything.

It is safe to ignore.

🧠 Important: Playground Is Deprecated

Apollo v5 no longer officially supports the old Playground.

If you want GraphQL UI in development, use:

Option 1 (Recommended): Apollo Sandbox (default)

Just enable introspection:

GraphQLModule.forRoot({
  autoSchemaFile: true,
  introspection: true,
});


Apollo Sandbox will appear automatically in dev.

Option 2: Use GraphiQL Instead

If you want modern UI without warnings.

